## Status: FIX APPLIED AND KEPT (no test regressions)

### Root cause
`dayOfWeek(year, month, day)` in `/luxon/src/impl/conversions.js` computed the weekday via `new Date(Date.UTC(year, month - 1, day)).getUTCDay()`. `Date.UTC` maps calendar years 0–99 to 19xx (legacy JS behavior), so for those years the weekday was wrong, which in turn corrupted `gregorianToWeek` (weekNumber/weekYear) and `weekToGregorian` (weekdayOfJan4). Scope measured: for years 1–105, **36,159 of 38,350 dates had a wrong weekday and 9,084 had wrong weekYear/weekNumber**; all 366 days of year 0 were wrong; the week↔gregorian round-trip was broken across the 100 barrier.

### Exact diff (only file I touched: `src/impl/conversions.js`)
```diff
 function dayOfWeek(year, month, day) {
-  const js = new Date(Date.UTC(year, month - 1, day)).getUTCDay();
+  const d = new Date(Date.UTC(year, month - 1, day));
+
+  if (year < 100 && year >= 0) {
+    // for legacy reasons, years between 0 and 99 are interpreted as 19XX; revert that
+    d.setUTCFullYear(year, month - 1, day);
+  }
+
+  const js = d.getUTCDay();
   return js === 0 ? 7 : js;
 }
```
(Same pattern as `objToLocalTS` in `src/impl/util.js`; re-setting month/day makes overflow normalize under the target year's own leap rules.) `npx prettier --list-different` and `npx eslint --quiet` are clean on the file. I did not touch `src/impl/util.js`, `src/interval.js`, `src/zones/fixedOffsetZone.js`, or any test file.

